summary:
- topic: New Superintendent
  text: The board unanimously approved the contract for new superintendent Dr. Angela
    Atkinson Dena, who will start on July 15th.
- topic: Kaler Reassignment Plan
  text: The main agenda item was the student attendance proposal for Kaler Elementary
    School, which is closing. The plan involves reassigning Kaler students to the
    four remaining elementary schools.
- topic: Community Feedback
  text: Kaler parents, especially from the Pleasantdale neighborhood, voiced strong
    opposition to the plan, citing the division of their community and the busing
    of children past closer schools.
- topic: Board Deliberation and Vote
  text: After extensive and divided discussion, the board initially defeated the proposal
    on a 3-3 vote. Following a successful motion to reconsider, the proposal was passed
    with a 5-1 vote.
- topic: Waiver & Transportation Commitment
  text: In passing the plan, the board stressed that the school choice waiver process
    would be prioritized for Kaler families, with a commitment to provide busing for
    approved waivers where possible.
- topic: Kaler Schedule Postponement
  text: A vote on a modified, shortened school year for Kaler Elementary School was
    postponed to a June 4th meeting to ensure adequate parent notification.
- topic: Transportation Issues
  text: Public comment raised concerns about the transportation department's failure
    to provide adequate busing for the SPHS and middle school bands for the Memorial
    Day parade.
- topic: Personnel Update
  text: The superintendent reported eight staff resignations across the district,
    including teachers and administrators.
